Borrower        Meridian Supply Co.
Facility        Committed revolving credit facility
Limit           $17,000,000
Tenor           36 months
Purpose         Working capital: to replace Meridian's short-term
                borrowing and to carry its receivables and stock as
                sales grow. Not for distributions or acquisitions.
Availability    The lesser of the limit and the borrowing base: 80%
                of eligible receivables plus 50% of eligible
                inventory, certified monthly.
Interest        Reference rate + 200 bps on amounts drawn
Fees            Commitment 70 bps a year on the undrawn limit;
                arrangement 0.50% of the limit.
Security        First-ranking security over all receivables,
                inventory and the collection account customers pay
                into; general security over other assets.
Guarantees      Every group company that holds receivables or
                inventory. No personal guarantee.
Ranking         Senior. Intercreditor agreement with the existing
                term lender: Fernhill first on receivables and
                stock, the term lender first on fixed assets.
Leverage        Debt / EBITDA no more than 3.25x
Interest cover  EBITDA / interest at least 4.00x
Distributions   Up to 35% of the previous year's net income, only
                with no default and leverage at or below 2.50x.
Reporting       borrowing base certificate and aged receivables
                monthly, within 20 days; management accounts and
                covenant certificate quarterly; audited accounts
                within 120 days of year end; a field examination of
                receivables and stock once a year
Conditions      audited 2025 accounts, not materially worse than the
                management accounts; aged receivables at 31 December
                2025 with ineligibles at or below 25%; short-term
                borrowing repaid and its security released;
                intercreditor agreement signed
